==English==
[[Image:Earthenware pottery for sale 2007.jpg|thumb|Earthenware pottery]]

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|earthen|-ware|id2=substance, kind, or use}}, first recorded appearance in 1673.<ref>''Chambers Dictionary of Etymology'', Robert K. Barnhart (ed.), Chambers, 1988</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈəːθ(ə)nwɛː/|ref={{R:Lexico}}|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-earthenware.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|ceramics|often|attributive}} An opaque, semi-porous [[ceramic]] made from clay and other compounds.
#: {{coordinate terms|en|stoneware}}
#: {{ux|en|'''earthenware''' bowl}}

